# The runtime dispatch path takes POSITIONAL arguments only, and refusing a
# keyword there is deliberate: pydyn_meth has parameter SLOTS and not the
# callee's parameter NAMES, so binding `k=v` to a position is precisely the
# mis-binding bug-nilpy-pyeval-fallback-still-binds-host-kwargs-by-position
# was about -- a wrong value, silently, in the caller's own argument order.
# Annotating the receiver resolves the call statically and has no such limit.


def f(o):
    return o.no_class_declares_this(k=1)


print(1)
